+      FIELD(conaffinity, "接触亲和力 (conaffinity)\n\n接触过滤用的 32 位掩码之一。两个几何体能否碰撞，取决于一方的 contype 与另一方的 conaffinity 是否有共同位同时为 1（反过来也一样）。\n\n官方原文：Bitmask for contact filtering; see contype above. Two geoms can collide if the contype of one geom is compatible with the conaffinity of the other geom or vice versa.");
+      FIELD(condim, "接触维度 (condim)\n\n接触空间的维度，取两个碰撞几何体中较大的那个 condim。\n\n官方原文：The dimensionality of the contact space for a dynamically generated contact pair is set to the maximum of the condim values of the two participating geoms. The allowed values and their meaning are: 1 = Frictionless contact. 3 = Regular frictional contact, opposing slip in the tangent plane. 4 = Frictional contact, opposing slip in the tangent plane and rotation around the contact normal.");
+      FIELD(priority, "优先级 (priority)\n\n接触优先级，决定两个几何体的属性如何合并成接触的属性。与「求解器混合 (solmix)」配合使用。\n\n官方原文：The geom priority determines how the properties of two colliding geoms are combined to form the properties of the contact. This interacts with the solmix attribute.");
+      FIELD(friction, "摩擦系数 (friction)\n\n接触摩擦系数，依次是滑动摩擦、滚动摩擦、自旋（扭转）摩擦。\n\n官方原文：Contact friction parameters for dynamically generated contact pairs. The first number is the sliding friction, acting along both axes of the tangent plane. The second number is the torsional friction, acting around the contact normal. The third number is the rolling friction, acting around both axes of the tangent plane.");
+      FIELD(solmix, "求解器混合 (solmix)\n\n接触参数的加权平均权重，与 priority 属性配合决定两个几何体的参数怎么合并。\n\n官方原文：This attribute specifies the weight used for averaging of contact parameters, and interacts with the priority attribute.");
+      FIELD(solref, "求解器参考 (solref)\n\n求解器参考参数（决定约束的刚度与阻尼）。含义与几何体的同名属性一致。\n\n官方原文：Same meaning as regular geom attributes.");
+      FIELD(solimp, "求解器阻抗 (solimp)\n\n接触仿真的约束求解器参数（阻抗部分）。\n\n官方原文：Constraint solver parameters for contact simulation.");
+      FIELD(margin, "检测边距 (margin)\n\n把几何体表面「膨胀」多少来提前产生接触力。两个表面距离小于 margin 就算激活、开始出力。求解器阻抗可以是距离的函数，作用于「两几何体距离减去 margin」。\n\n官方原文：Geometric inflation of the geom surface for the purpose of contact force generation. When the distance between two geom surfaces is below margin, the contact is considered active and contact forces are generated. The constraint impedance can be a function of distance.");
+      FIELD(gap, "间隙 (gap)\n\n在 margin 之外再多探一段的缓冲距离。为正时：距离 margin+gap 就开始检测，但只有到了 margin 才真正产生力。夹在两者之间的接触以「非激活接触」形式记录在 mjData.contact 里（efc_address = -1），可供自定义计算使用。\n\n官方原文：Additional contact detection buffer beyond margin. When this value is positive, contacts are detected at distance margin + gap but forces are only generated at distance margin.");
+      FIELD(dim, "维度 (dim)\n\n柔性体的维度。1 = 一维（元素是胶囊），2 = 二维（元素是带半径的三角形），3 = 三维（元素是带可选半径的四面体）。\n\n官方原文：Dimensionality of the flex. Allowed values are 1, 2 and 3. In 1D the elements are capsules, in 2D the elements are triangles with radius, in 3D the elements are tetrahedra with (optional) radius.");
+      FIELD(radius, "半径 (radius)\n\n柔性体所有元素的半径。三维下可以为零，一维和二维必须为正。半径同时影响碰撞检测和渲染；一维/二维靠它才有体积。\n\n官方原文：Radius of all flex elements. It can be zero in 3D, but must be positive in 1D and 2D. The radius affects both collision detection and rendering. In 1D and 2D it is needed to make the elements volumetric.");
+      FIELD(size, "尺寸 (size)\n\n在参考构型 qpos0 下，柔性体顶点包围盒的半宽（三个方向）。\n\n官方原文：vertex bounding box half sizes in qpos0（Studio 自带 tooltip，官方文档无独立说明）");
+      FIELD(internal, "内部 (internal)\n\n是否启用柔性体内部碰撞检测（防止自穿透和单元翻转）。共顶点的单元之间不会碰撞，否则会永久接触。\n\n官方原文：Enables or disables internal collisions which prevent flex self-penetration and element inversion. Note that flex elements that have shared vertices cannot collide (or else there will be permanent contacts).");
+      FIELD(flatskin, "扁平蒙皮 (flatskin)\n\n以 flexskin 方式渲染的二/三维柔性体用平滑着色还是平面着色。默认的平滑着色适合大多数情况；如果物体本身有明显棱角（比如立方体），平面着色更自然。\n\n官方原文：This attribute determines whether 2D and 3D flexes that are rendered in flexskin mode will use smooth or flat shading. The default smooth shading is suitable in most cases, however if the object is intended to have visible sharp edges (such as a cube) then flat shading is more natural.");
+      FIELD(selfcollide, "自碰撞 (selfcollide)\n\n同一柔性体内部元素之间怎么筛掉不可能碰撞的对：none = 完全不互相碰撞；narrow = 只做精确检测（所有对都查，仅供诊断，实用中不可取）；bvh / sap = 先用包围体层次或扫描-剪枝做粗筛。\n\n官方原文：This determines the strategy for midphase collision pruning of element pairs belonging to the same flex. none means flex elements cannot collide with each other. narrow means narrow phase only (i.e. all pairs are checked). This is a diagnostic tool and is never a good idea in practice. bvh and sap refer to bounding volume hierarchies and sweep-and-prune.");
+      FIELD(passive, "被动 (passive)\n\n开启后，接触不进接触求解器，而是改用被动（弹簧-阻尼）接触力计算。此时无论 condim 设为多少，接触都是无摩擦的（condim 1）。这是实验性功能。\n\n官方原文：When enabled, the contact is not added to the contact solver but it is instead used to compute passive (spring-damper) contact forces. All contacts, regardless of the specified condim, are frictionless (condim 1). This is an experimental feature.");
+      FIELD(activelayers, "激活层 (activelayers)\n\n只对三维柔性体有效。编译器会给每个四面体标一个整数 = 它到柔性体外表面的图距离：贴表面的在第 0 层，邻居第 1 层，依此类推。这个值决定允许参与碰撞的层数，默认 1 表示只有最外层参与。\n\n官方原文：This only has an effect for 3D flexes. Each tetrahedron is labeled by the model compiler with an integer corresponding to (graph) distance to the outside surface of the flex. Thus outside-facing elements are in layer 0, their neighbors are in layer 1, etc. This attribute specifies how many layers will be allowed to participate in collisions.");
+      FIELD(group, "分组 (group)\n\n整数分组号，用于可视化时成组开关显示。\n\n官方原文：Integer group to which the skin belongs. This attribute can be used for custom tags. It is also used by the visualizer to enable and disable the rendering of entire groups of skins.");
+      FIELD(edgestiffness, "边刚度 (edgestiffness)\n\n柔性体各条边的刚度系数（与「边阻尼」配对，共同决定边弹簧-阻尼器的行为）。\n\n官方原文：edge stiffness（Studio 自带 tooltip；官方文档此处无可摘录原句）");
